From: Kenichi Kamiya <kachick1@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] options: prefetch flake store path if unmaterialized (Nix 2.35 lazy-trees)

In Nix 2.35, lazy-trees became the default behavior, so `nix flake metadata`
no longer materializes the git tree in /nix/store/. Downstream evaluation
via `eval.nix` fails with "No such file or directory" when reading the
store path.

If the store path reported by `nix flake metadata` does not exist on disk,
run `nix flake prefetch` to realize it.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/Mic92/nix-update/issues/687
---
 nix_update/options.py | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/nix_update/options.py b/nix_update/options.py
--- a/nix_update/options.py
+++ b/nix_update/options.py
@@ -122,6 +122,14 @@ def get_flake_store_path(import_path: str) -> str | None:
         if not isinstance(path, str):
             return None
 
+        if not Path(path).exists():
+            subprocess.run(
+                ["nix", "flake", "prefetch"],
+                cwd=import_path,
+                capture_output=True,
+                check=True,
+            )
+
         flake_dir = _metadata_flake_dir(metadata)
         if flake_dir:
             return str(Path(path) / flake_dir)
-- 
